        "history":  "\u003cstrong\u003eHistorical Context\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eIn the late 1990s, the portable market was overwhelmingly dominated by Game Boy Color. No other company had managed to significantly penetrate this market. SNK, recognized for arcade quality and Neo Geo AES, wanted to bring fighting game quality to the portable segment — a niche uncovered by Game Boy, which had never excelled in fighting games.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eConsole Development\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eNeo Geo Pocket was designed around a microswitch joystick with a distinct tactile feel — a deliberate choice over Game Boy\u0027s standard D-pad. The Toshiba TLCS-900H processor at 6.144 MHz, 12 KB RAM, and a custom GPU produced 160×152 monochrome pixels. Battery life of over 30 hours on two AA batteries represented a clear advantage over Game Gear.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eLaunch\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eNeo Geo Pocket was launched in March 1998 in Japan at 7,800 yen. Exclusive titles like King of Fighters R-1, Fatal Fury: First Contact, and Samurai Shodown! constituted the main attraction. The console was monochrome — a limitation compared to Game Boy Color, which had already appeared on the market with a color screen.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eMarket Impact\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eNeo Geo Pocket sold approximately 1.2 million units — a modest figure compared to the 118+ million of the Game Boy line. The monochrome screen placed the console at an immediate disadvantage against Game Boy Color, launched a few months later. The public was not convinced to abandon the Nintendo ecosystem for an alternative with a limited library.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eLegacy\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eNeo Geo Pocket remained in industry history as a product with excellent design — the microswitch joystick is praised by collectors to this day — but with poor timing and wrong market. SNK quickly followed with Neo Geo Pocket Color (1999), but could not fundamentally change the balance. NGP\u0027s mechanical joystick indirectly influenced the design of some later controllers and remains a preference of fighting game enthusiasts.",
