        "history":  "\u003cstrong\u003eHistorical Context\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eIn the early 2000s, PlayStation 2 had already dominated the market with integrated DVD and a massive library inherited from PS1. Microsoft had announced Xbox, its first direct competitor in the console market. Nintendo, with N64 approaching retirement, needed to respond with a sixth-generation console capable of competing with both rivals, while maintaining its identity as a gameplay-centered platform.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eConsole Development\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eGameCube was project \u0027Dolphin\u0027, developed in partnership with ArtX and IBM. The IBM Gekko CPU at 485 MHz and ATI Flipper GPU at 162 MHz, backed by 24 MB MoSys 1T-SRAM RAM, 3 MB video, and 16 MB A/D Buffer, delivered real-world performance of 6–12 million polygons per second. The console abandoned cartridges for GameCube Game Disc (8 cm, 1.5 GB) — a proprietary format that prevented piracy but limited capacity versus DVD. The cuboid design of 11.4 × 15 × 16 cm included a handle for portability. The controller reinvented ergonomics: oversized A button in the center, analog L/R triggers, and C-Stick. WaveBird (2002) introduced wireless via RF without line of sight.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eLaunch\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eGameCube was launched in Japan on September 14, 2001, in North America on November 18, 2001, and in Europe on May 3, 2002, at $199. Super Smash Bros. Melee as a launch title demonstrated graphical performance. Connectivity with Game Boy Advance — GBA as a secondary screen — and Game Boy Player for running portable games on TV completed the ecosystem.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eMarket Impact\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eGameCube sold approximately 22 million units, finishing the generation in third place after PS2 (160+ million) and Xbox (24 million). The library included exceptional titles — Super Smash Bros. Melee, Mario Kart: Double Dash!!, The Wind Waker, Resident Evil 4, and Luigi\u0027s Mansion — but the absence of video DVD weakened multimedia positioning, and PS2\u0027s temporal advantage eroded appeal to the general public. The \u0027toy\u0027 perception limited attracting the adult demographic.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eLegacy\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eGameCube was the last Nintendo console to compete directly on raw hardware specifications. Its lessons led to the company\u0027s \u0027Blue Ocean\u0027 strategy — instead of competing on power, Nintendo chose gameplay innovation through Wii. The GameCube controller is appreciated to this day for its ergonomics, and Super Smash Bros. Melee remains one of the most played competitive titles in console history.",
