        "history":  "\u003cstrong\u003eHistorical Context\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eIn the mid-2000s, PlayStation 2 dominated the market with 160+ million units. The original Xbox had proven that Microsoft could compete, but had lost to Sony in sales volume. Nintendo and Sony were preparing their next consoles, and Microsoft chose to launch Xbox 360 a year ahead of the competition — a \u0027first mover advantage\u0027 strategy to win the user base before PS3 was available.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eConsole Development\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eXbox 360 abandoned the original\u0027s PC-type architecture for a custom solution: the IBM \u0027Xenon\u0027 triple-core processor at 3.2 GHz capable of running six execution threads, ATI \u0027Xenos\u0027 GPU at 500 MHz with 10 MB eDRAM and 240 shader units. Memory was doubled to 512 MB GDDR3 at Epic Games\u0027 request — a decision that cost approximately one billion dollars but ensured the platform\u0027s long-term viability. Xbox 360 supported native HD resolutions: 720p, 1080i, and later 1080p. The \u0027Achievements\u0027 system with Gamerscore points created a new type of engagement, quickly adopted by the entire industry.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eLaunch\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eXbox 360 was launched on November 22, 2005, at $299 (Arcade) and $399 (Premium). Halo 3 (2007) generated $170 million on its first day. Kinect (2010), launched under the codename \u0027Project Natal\u0027, became the fastest-selling consumer electronics device in history at that time. Xbox Live Arcade revolutionized digital distribution for indie and retro games.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eMarket Impact\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eXbox 360 sold over 84 million units, consolidating Microsoft as a major player alongside Sony and Nintendo. The \u0027Red Ring of Death\u0027 crisis — GPU solder joint fracturing due to thermal stress — cost Microsoft $1.15 billion in extended warranties and repairs, but the rapid and transparent response allowed the platform to maintain momentum. Xbox Live surpassed 30 million subscribers in 2011.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eLegacy\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eXbox 360 defined the online services paradigm for consoles and established modern standards for digital distribution, community engagement through Achievements, and the living room multimedia hub. Xbox Live Arcade pioneered the indie game platform, foreshadowing the dominant digital distribution model of today. Production ceased on April 20, 2016, but the library remains accessible through the backward compatibility program on Xbox Series X/S.",
