        "history":  "\u003cstrong\u003eHistorical Context\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eIn the mid-2000s, the console market was dominated by Xbox 360 and PlayStation 3 — both pursuing maximum hardware power, HD screens, and online services. Nintendo had finished the GameCube generation in third place and was looking for a radically different direction. Satoru Iwata promoted the \u0027Blue Ocean\u0027 philosophy — instead of competing with Sony and Microsoft on the same ground, Nintendo wanted to create a new market, attracting audiences who had never played video games.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eConsole Development\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWii was designed around motion control as the central element: Wii Remote based on accelerometer and infrared sensor, with MotionPlus adding gyroscopic precision. The IBM Broadway CPU at 729 MHz and ATI Hollywood GPU at 243 MHz offered performance equivalent to GameCube — deliberately inferior to Xbox 360 and PS3 to reduce costs. The console was limited to 480p (NTSC) — without native HD output. The RVL-001 model maintained complete compatibility with GameCube games. Internal storage of 512 MB flash was expandable with SD card.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eLaunch\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWii was launched in North America on November 19, 2006, at $249.99, alongside Wii Sports — a pack of five demonstration games for motion control. Wii Sports became the platform\u0027s symbol, selling 82.9 million copies — the best-selling single-platform game in history. Stock shortages persisted for months after launch.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eMarket Impact\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWii sold 101.63 million units — the second best-selling of the generation after Nintendo DS. It surpassed both Xbox 360 and PlayStation 3 in global volume. Balance Board, used for fitness and medical rehabilitation, extended Wii beyond gaming. Games like Super Mario Galaxy, The Legend of Zelda: Twilight Princess, and Metroid Prime 3 demonstrated that gameplay innovation can coexist with first-party quality.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eLegacy\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWii demonstrated that a console can win the global market without being the most powerful of its generation. It expanded the video game audience to new publics — families, seniors, people with disabilities — validating the \u0027Blue Ocean\u0027 philosophy. Wii\u0027s lessons directly influenced Nintendo Switch (2017) and the entire industry\u0027s approach to accessibility. Today, the RVL-001 model remains valuable to collectors due to native GameCube compatibility.",
