        "history":  "\u003cstrong\u003eHistorical Context\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eIn the early 2010s, Nintendo DS had dominated the portable market, and PSP had sold well but lost the battle against DS. Sony wanted to create the PSP successor that would truly deliver the home console experience in portable format — an ambition PSP had approached but not fully achieved. iPhone and Android smartphones were rapidly gaining share in the mobile gaming market, creating additional pressure.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eConsole Development\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003ePlayStation Vita was designed as the most powerful handheld ever created: ARM Cortex-A9 quad-core processor at 2 GHz, PowerVR SGX543MP4+ GPU with 512 MB RAM, and a 5-inch OLED screen at 960×544 pixels (220 ppi) on the original PCH-1000 model. Dual analog sticks, front resistive touchscreen, rear touchpad, full Sixaxis sensors (gyroscope and accelerometer), and Wi-Fi/Bluetooth/3G connectivity completed an unprecedented technical package for a handheld. Remote Play allowed streaming from PS3 and later PS4.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eLaunch\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eVita was launched in Japan in December 2011 and globally in February 2012 at $249.99. Uncharted: Golden Abyss immediately demonstrated the graphical quality. Proprietary memory cards — required for saves and digital content — immediately became the main point of criticism: 32 GB cost $120, nearly half the console\u0027s price.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eMarket Impact\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eVita sold 15–16 million units — a commercial failure compared to PSP\u0027s 80+ million. Sony officially declared in 2015 that it would no longer develop AAA games for Vita. Expensive proprietary memory cards, lack of consistent first-party support, and smartphone competition eroded platform adoption. The SD2Vita adapter, developed by the modding community, later solved the proprietary card problem through standard microSD usage.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eLegacy\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003ePlayStation Vita remains a paradox: the most powerful handheld of its generation, but a commercial failure caused by wrong strategic decisions. The platform built a devoted indie and JRPG community that continues to be active in 2026. In the words of analysts: „PS Vita didn\u0027t fail Sony; Sony failed PS Vita.”",
