        "history":  "\u003cstrong\u003eHistorical Context\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eIn the early 2010s, PlayStation 3 was finishing the generation with solid performance, but with a complicated reputation — the high initial price, the difficult Cell architecture, and Xbox 360\u0027s one-year head start had cost Sony important market share. Microsoft had announced Xbox One with controversies related to DRM and mandatory internet connection. Sony identified the opportunity to return to the top of the industry with a simple message: for gamers, without restrictions.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eConsole Development\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003ePS4 was designed with a semi-custom AMD Jaguar APU with 8 cores at 1.6 GHz and AMD Radeon GPU at 1.84 TFLOPS — a completely new x86-64 architecture compared to Cell, much easier to program. 8 GB GDDR5 at 176 GB/s offered exceptional bandwidth. A 500 GB or 1 TB HDD at 5,400 RPM, Blu-ray drive, and USB 3.0 port completed the configuration. DualShock 4 added a touchpad, LED light bar, and Share button for screenshot capture and streaming. The optional PlayStation Camera enabled PlayStation VR.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eLaunch\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003ePS4 was announced in February 2013 and launched in North America on November 15, 2013, at $399 — $100 less than Xbox One. The E3 2013 message — a video simply demonstrating physical game sharing — went immediately viral, winning a perception battle against Microsoft. Killzone: Shadow Fall and Resogun were the launch titles.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eMarket Impact\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003ePS4 sold over 117 million units — the second best-selling home console in Sony history, after PS2. Defining exclusives — The Last of Us Part II, God of War (2018), Horizon Zero Dawn, Spider-Man, Ghost of Tsushima, and Death Stranding — set the standards for single-player cinematic games. PS4 Pro (2016) brought 4K checkerboard rendering and HDR. PlayStation VR (2016) was the first accessible VR initiative on a mainstream console.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eLegacy\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003ePS4 repositioned Sony as the undisputed leader of the generation, returning to first place after a difficult generation with PS3. It demonstrated that clear marketing messaging — „for gamers” — can be just as important as hardware specifications. The PS4 library remains accessible through backward compatibility on PS5, and in 2026 the console continues to offer access to cross-gen titles at reduced prices.",
