        "history":  "\u003cstrong\u003eHistorical Context\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eIn the early 2010s, Xbox 360 had finished the generation in second place behind PS3 in global volumes, but had dominated North America. Microsoft wanted to transform Xbox One not just into a console, but into the central multimedia hub of the living room — a single device for games, television, movies, and music. The improved Kinect 2.0 was conceived as the central element of the experience, not an optional accessory.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eConsole Development\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eXbox One used an AMD Jaguar CPU with 8 cores at 1.75 GHz and GCN 1.1 GPU at 1.3 TFLOPS — inferior to PS4 (1.84 TFLOPS). 8 GB DDR3 and HDMI-In for TV integration completed a device designed as a multimedia center. Kinect 2.0 was mandatory at launch, increasing the price. The family evolved significantly: Xbox One S (2016) added HDR10 support and 4K UHD Blu-ray playback; Xbox One X (2017) reached 6 TFLOPS for native 4K performance; Xbox One S All-Digital removed the optical drive.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eLaunch\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eXbox One was launched on November 22, 2013, at $499 — $100 more than PS4 — including Kinect 2.0. Pre-launch controversies regarding DRM and mandatory internet connection generated strong negative reactions, forcing Microsoft to cancel those policies. Titanfall (2014) was the first major exclusive title, but appeared simultaneously on Xbox 360.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eMarket Impact\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eXbox One sold approximately 50 million units — less than PS4 (117 million). However, Xbox Game Pass — introduced in 2017 — changed the platform\u0027s business model, offering access to a vast library through a monthly subscription. Backward compatibility with Xbox 360 and original Xbox was a unique differentiator versus PS4, which didn\u0027t offer backward compatibility.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eLegacy\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eXbox One lost the sales battle against PS4, but won the battle of the future through Game Pass. The subscription service redefined the game distribution model and directly influenced Xbox Series X/S. Extended backward compatibility across three Xbox generations remains a distinct advantage of the Microsoft ecosystem over the competition.",
