        "history":  "\u003cstrong\u003eHistorical Context\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eIn the mid-2010s, Nintendo was in a difficult position: Wii U had failed commercially with 13.56 million units, and 3DS was in decline. The portable console market was threatened by smartphones, and the home console market was dominated by PS4 and Xbox One. Nintendo needed to completely reinvent the hardware formula and find a concept that would work simultaneously in both segments.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eConsole Development\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eNintendo Switch was designed as a hybrid console: a portable device that connected to TV through a dock. The NVIDIA Tegra X1 processor at 1.02 GHz (portable) and 1.02 GHz (docked) and NVIDIA Maxwell GPU with 256 CUDA cores at 768 MHz provided an energy-efficient platform. Detachable Joy-Con with HD Rumble (granular haptic feedback), IR camera, and motion sensors completed the interaction innovation. Nintendo Switch Online offered access to classic NES, SNES, and later N64 and Game Boy games. The Joy-Con drift problem — analog stick axis wear — became a persistent sensitive point of the platform.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eLaunch\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eNintendo Switch was launched globally on March 3, 2017, at $299.99. The Legend of Zelda: Breath of the Wild as the launch title received universal 10/10 reviews and immediately demonstrated that Nintendo had not given up on creative ambitions. Super Mario Odyssey (October 2017), Mario Kart 8 Deluxe, and Splatoon 2 consolidated the launch. Switch OLED (2021) brought a larger 7-inch screen, and Switch Lite (2019) a more affordable exclusively portable variant.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eMarket Impact\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eNintendo Switch sold 155.37 million units by the end of 2025 — surpassing Nintendo DS and becoming the best-selling Nintendo console in history. Animal Crossing: New Horizons (2020) sold 43+ million copies, becoming a global cultural phenomenon amplified by the COVID-19 pandemic. Mario Kart 8 Deluxe sold 67+ million copies — the best-selling game in Nintendo history.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eLegacy\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eNintendo Switch definitively validated the hybrid console concept as a major industry direction. It demonstrated that user experience and accessibility can surpass competitors\u0027 technical advantages. Nintendo Switch 2, launched in June 2025, continues this philosophy with a significant technological leap, confirming that hybridity has become the central identity of the Nintendo brand.",
