        "history":  "\u003cstrong\u003eHistorical Context\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eIn the late 2010s, PlayStation 4 had dominated the generation with 117+ million units, but was limited by its slow mechanical HDD, insufficient graphical power for native 4K at 60 fps, and lack of hardware ray tracing. Xbox Series X announced 12 TFLOPS versus PS4 Pro\u0027s 1.84 TFLOPS. Sony needed to respond with a console that would eliminate loading times — the main frustration cited by players — and offer authentic 4K graphical quality.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eConsole Development\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003ePS5 was built around a custom PCIe 4.0 SSD at 5.5 GB/s raw (8–9 GB/s effective with compression) — 100 times faster than the PS4\u0027s HDD. AMD Zen 2 CPU with 8 cores at variable 3.5 GHz and RDNA 2 GPU with 36 CU at 2.23 GHz delivering 10.28 TFLOPS, with hardware ray tracing and Variable Rate Shading. 16 GB GDDR6 at 448 GB/s completed a modern platform. Tempest 3D Audio provides spatial sound without special equipment. DualSense introduced adaptive triggers (variable resistance) and granular haptic feedback — a complete reinvention of the controller compared to DualShock 4.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eLaunch\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003ePS5 was launched on November 12, 2020, in North America at $499 (with disc) and $399 (Digital Edition). Demand massively exceeded supply for the first 18 months due to semiconductor shortages. Spider-Man: Miles Morales and Demon\u0027s Souls Remake were the defining launch titles. PS5 Slim (2023) reduced dimensions, and PS5 Pro (2024) added +45% GPU power and 2–3x faster ray tracing.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eMarket Impact\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003ePS5 surpassed 50 million units sold by 2024. Sony exclusives — Returnal, Ratchet \u0026 Clank: Rift Apart, Horizon Forbidden West, God of War: Ragnarok, Spider-Man 2 — leveraged the SSD and DualSense for previously impossible experiences. Backward compatibility with over 99% of the PS4 library ensured a frictionless transition.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eLegacy\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003ePS5 demonstrated that a fast SSD can be just as transformative as a generational leap in raw power. DualSense redefined controller feedback and influenced future controller design. Tempest 3D Audio and hardware ray tracing established new immersion standards. PlayStation 6 is anticipated for 2027–2028, and PS5 has a solid usage and commercial support cycle in 2026.",
