        "history":  "\u003cstrong\u003eHistorical Context\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eIn the mid-2020s, Nintendo Switch — launched in 2017 — had accumulated 155+ million units sold and became the best-selling Nintendo console in history. The Tegra X1 processor, performant in 2017, had become visibly outdated compared to modern PC handhelds and PS5/Xbox Series. Major titles like Hogwarts Legacy and many others hadn\u0027t been ported to Switch for technical reasons. Nintendo needed to make a generational leap that would maintain the hybrid philosophy, backward compatibility, and open the platform for a new category of titles.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eConsole Development\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eNintendo Switch 2 (internal code „Ounce”) was designed around the NVIDIA Tegra T239 (Drake) processor with Ampere architecture — a massive leap from Tegra X1. The octa-core ARM Cortex-A78C processor, 1,536 CUDA cores with Ray Tracing and DLSS support, 12 GB LPDDR5X RAM, and 256 GB UFS 3.1 storage formed the technical core. The 7.9-inch LCD screen with 120 Hz refresh rate and HDR10 support offered a notably superior visual experience. A dedicated hardware decompression engine (FDE) handled compressed files, reducing loading times. Joy-Con 2 used strong magnets instead of the rail system — producing a characteristic snap sound when connecting — and a C button for quick GameChat access.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eLaunch\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eNintendo Switch 2 was launched globally on June 5, 2025, at $449.99, with premium games reaching $80. Mario Kart World as the launch title sold over 14 million units in the first months. The console reached 17.37 million units sold by the end of 2025 — the fastest debut in Nintendo history. GameChat (voice, video, and screen sharing) was the services innovation, responding to the social communication need identified during the pandemic period.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eMarket Impact\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eNintendo Switch 2 demonstrated that the market accepted the Switch model at a higher price, with premium games and significantly improved hardware. DLSS enables 4K at 60 fps in docked mode — an experience impossible on Switch 1. Backward compatibility with most Switch 1 games — with graphical updates for major titles — ensured a frictionless transition. Nintendo Classics brought GameCube games to the platform through Nintendo Switch Online.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eLegacy\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eNintendo Switch 2 validates hybridity as the central and permanent direction for Nintendo — not a temporary experiment, but a brand identity. Magnetic Joy-Con, GameChat, and DLSS represent evolutions that keep the product technologically relevant without abandoning fundamental principles: accessibility, portability, and local multiplayer. Nintendo Switch 2 enters 2026 with a solid commercial cycle and a rapidly expanding library.",
